//? Title: Quadratic sieve: actual smooth relations, parity pivots and square dependencies
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Factoring an integer can be reduced to finding two different square roots of the
same residue. The quadratic sieve collects smooth values of x squared minus n,
cancels their exponent parity and extracts a gcd from the resulting congruence
of squares. This report reads actual native relations and dependencies, keeps
the original four semiprimes, and distinguishes a successful factor from an
exhausted bounded search.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

A positive smooth value has \(x_i^2-n=\prod_j p_j^{e_{ij}}\). Select relation
rows whose exponent vectors sum to zero modulo two. Their full exponent sums are
even, hence
$$ X=\prod_i x_i\pmod n,\quad Y=\prod_j p_j^{\frac12\sum_i e_{ij}}\pmod n,\quad X^2\equiv Y^2\pmod n. $$
\alttext(Even exponent sums turn the selected smooth product into a square congruence.)
Thus \(n\) divides \((X-Y)(X+Y)\); a gcd of the actual difference may reveal a
nontrivial factor. The gcd can also be1 or n, so a dependency is not itself a
success certificate. Incremental GF2 elimination records actual pivot columns
and selected relation ids. Root-directed sieving removes base primes, followed
by full exponent reconstruction before accepting any relation.

General quadratic-sieve asymptotics rely on heuristic smoothness estimates and
scalable arbitrary-precision implementations. This uint64 implementation has a
bounded factor base/window search. Its measured selected counts are not the old
drawn subexponential reference curve, and an exhausted budget does not certify
primality.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/quadratic_sieve_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/prufer.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/flow_diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/hull_algorithms.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/sampling_analysis.hpp>
#include <iomanip>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/quadratic_sieve.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    a::QuadraticSieveOptions o;
    o.factor_base_bound = 3;
    auto t = a::quadratic_sieve_trace(77, o);
    const auto &dep = t.dependencies[0];
    std::print("\n| actual relation id | x | actual factor-base exponents | pivot column |\n| ---: | ---: | " "--- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.relations.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` | {} |\n", i, t.relations[i].x,
                   t.relations[i].exponents, t.relations[i].pivot_column);
    std::print("Actual factor base: {}. Dependency member ids: {}.\n",
               t.factor_base, dep.members);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual smooth x / n\n{} / 77", t.relations[0].x));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual square residues\nX={}, Y={}", dep.X, dep.Y));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0}, std::format("Actual gcd factor\n{}", dep.gcd));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/quadratic_sieve_tiny.svg");
}
```
